{"Title":"Cyrena.Persistence.File","Keywords":["Cyrena.Persistence.File","FileStore","PersistenceFS","FilePersistenceBuilder","FilePersistenceOptions","IPersistenceFS","file persistence","JSON storage","UseFilePersistence","AddFilePersistence","AddIsolatedFilePersistence"],"Summary":"JSON file-based persistence implementation for Cyrena. Provides FileStore\u003CT\u003E implementing IStore\u003CT\u003E, PersistenceFS for file system operations, and builder extensions for configuring file-based storage.","Link":null,"Content":"## Overview\n\n\u0060Cyrena.Persistence.File\u0060 is the JSON file-based persistence implementation for the Cyr\u00E9na framework. It provides concrete implementations of the persistence contracts defined in \u0060Cyrena.Persistence.Core\u0060, storing entities as individual JSON files in a directory structure.\n\n**Version:** 0.6.0\n**Target Framework:** .NET 10.0\n**Namespaces:** \u0060Cyrena.Contracts\u0060, \u0060Cyrena.Extensions\u0060, \u0060Cyrena.Options\u0060, \u0060Cyrena.Persistence.File.Options\u0060, \u0060Cyrena.Persistence.File.Services\u0060, \u0060Cyrena.Services\u0060\n\n---\n\n## Contracts\n\n### \u0060IPersistenceFS\u0060\nFile system abstraction for reading, writing, and deleting entity JSON files.\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\npublic interface IPersistenceFS\n{\n    IList\u003CT\u003E Read\u003CT\u003E(string collectionName) where T : class, IEntity;\n    void Write\u003CT\u003E(T entity, string collectionName) where T : class, IEntity;\n    void Delete\u003CT\u003E(string id, string collectionName) where T : class, IEntity;\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**Methods:**\n- \u0060Read\u003CT\u003E\u0060: Loads all entities from a collection directory, deserializing JSON files.\n- \u0060Write\u003CT\u003E\u0060: Writes an entity to a JSON file (creates or updates).\n- \u0060Delete\u003CT\u003E\u0060: Removes an entity\u0027s JSON file by ID.\n\n---\n\n## Services\n\n### \u0060FileStore\u003CT\u003E\u0060 (internal)\nImplements \u0060IStore\u003CT\u003E\u0060 using \u0060IPersistenceFS\u0060 for JSON file storage.\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\ninternal class FileStore\u003CT\u003E : IStore\u003CT\u003E where T : class, IEntity\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**Constructors:**\n- \u0060FileStore(IPersistenceFS fs)\u0060 \u2014 Uses \u0060typeof(T).Name\u0060 as collection name\n- \u0060FileStore(IPersistenceFS fs, string collectionName)\u0060 \u2014 Uses explicit collection name\n\n**Key behaviors:**\n- Auto-generates \u0060Guid.NewGuid().ToString()\u0060 for null IDs on \u0060AddAsync\u0060 and \u0060SaveAsync\u0060\n- \u0060QueryableData\u0060 reads from \u0060_fs.Read\u003CT\u003E(_collectionName)\u0060 and converts to \u0060IQueryable\u0060\n- \u0060FindManyAsync\u0060 supports \u0060IOrderBy\u003CT\u003E\u0060 (ascending/descending) and \u0060IPaging\u0060 (Skip/Take)\n- \u0060DeleteManyAsync\u0060 evaluates specification, deletes matching files, returns count\n- \u0060Dispose()\u0060 is a no-op\n\n**Thread safety:** Relies on \u0060PersistenceFS\u0060 lock mechanism.\n\n### \u0060PersistenceFS\u0060 (internal)\nConcrete \u0060IPersistenceFS\u0060 implementation with in-memory caching and file I/O.\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\ninternal class PersistenceFS : IPersistenceFS\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**Constructors:**\n- \u0060PersistenceFS(IOptions\u003CFilePersistenceOptions\u003E options)\u0060 \u2014 From DI options\n- \u0060PersistenceFS(FilePersistenceOptions options)\u0060 \u2014 Direct options instance\n\n**Key behaviors:**\n- Maintains an in-memory cache (\u0060Dictionary\u003Cstring, IList\u003CIEntity\u003E\u003E\u0060) per collection\n- Thread-safe via \u0060lock (_lock)\u0060 on all operations\n- \u0060Read\u003CT\u003E\u0060: Returns cached collection if available; otherwise loads from disk, caches, and returns\n- \u0060Write\u003CT\u003E\u0060: Updates in-memory cache and writes indented JSON to file\n- \u0060Delete\u003CT\u003E\u0060: Removes from in-memory cache and deletes file if exists\n- JSON files are written with \u0060WriteIndented = true\u0060 for readability\n\n**File layout:**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n{BaseDirectory}/\n  {collectionName}/\n    {entityId}.json\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n---\n\n## Options\n\n### \u0060FilePersistenceOptions\u0060\nConfiguration for file-based persistence.\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\npublic class FilePersistenceOptions\n{\n    public string BaseDirectory { get; set; } = \u0022./data\u0022;\n    public string FileExtension { get; set; } = \u0022json\u0022;\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n| Property | Default | Description |\n|----------|---------|-------------|\n| \u0060BaseDirectory\u0060 | \u0060\u0022./data\u0022\u0060 | Root directory for all collection folders |\n| \u0060FileExtension\u0060 | \u0060\u0022json\u0022\u0060 | File extension for entity JSON files |\n\n---\n\n## Builders\n\n### \u0060FilePersistenceBuilder\u0060 (internal)\nImplements \u0060ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder\u0060 for standard (shared \u0060PersistenceFS\u0060) file storage.\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\ninternal class FilePersistenceBuilder : ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n- \u0060AddScopedStore\u003CTEntity\u003E\u0060: Registers \u0060IStore\u003CTEntity\u003E\u0060 as scoped, resolving \u0060IPersistenceFS\u0060 from DI\n- \u0060AddSingletonStore\u003CTEntity\u003E\u0060: Registers \u0060IStore\u003CTEntity\u003E\u0060 as singleton, resolving \u0060IPersistenceFS\u0060 from DI\n\n### \u0060IsolatedFilePersistenceBuilder\u0060 (internal)\nImplements \u0060ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder\u0060 for isolated (per-kernel) file storage.\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\ninternal class IsolatedFilePersistenceBuilder : ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n- Creates a dedicated \u0060PersistenceFS\u0060 instance with its own \u0060FilePersistenceOptions\u0060\n- \u0060AddScopedStore\u003CTEntity\u003E\u0060: Registers \u0060IStore\u003CTEntity\u003E\u0060 as scoped with isolated \u0060PersistenceFS\u0060\n- \u0060AddSingletonStore\u003CTEntity\u003E\u0060: Registers \u0060IStore\u003CTEntity\u003E\u0060 as singleton with isolated \u0060PersistenceFS\u0060\n\n**Use case:** Per-kernel isolated storage where data should not be shared across kernels.\n\n---\n\n## Extension Methods\n\n### \u0060CyrenaBuilderExtensions.UseFilePersistence\u0060\nConfigures file-based persistence at the application level.\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\npublic static class CyrenaBuilderExtensions\n{\n    public static CyrenaBuilder UseFilePersistence(this CyrenaBuilder builder, Action\u003CFilePersistenceOptions\u003E options);\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**What it does:**\n1. Creates \u0060FilePersistenceBuilder\u0060 and registers it as \u0060ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder\u0060 in \u0060FeatureOptions\u0060\n2. Registers \u0060IPersistenceFS\u0060 as singleton \u0060PersistenceFS\u0060\n3. Configures \u0060FilePersistenceOptions\u0060 via the action callback\n\n**Usage:**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\nbuilder.UseFilePersistence(options =\u003E\n{\n    options.BaseDirectory = \u0022./my-data\u0022;\n    options.FileExtension = \u0022json\u0022;\n});\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n### \u0060KernelBuilderExtensions.AddFilePersistence\u0060\nConfigures file-based persistence scoped to a specific kernel/chat.\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\npublic static class KernelBuilderExtensions\n{\n    public static ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder AddFilePersistence(\n        this CyrenaKernelBuilder builder, string path, string extension = \u0022json\u0022);\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**What it does:**\n1. Configures \u0060FilePersistenceOptions\u0060 with the provided path and extension\n2. Registers \u0060IPersistenceFS\u0060 as singleton \u0060PersistenceFS\u0060\n3. Creates \u0060FilePersistenceBuilder\u0060 and registers it as \u0060ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder\u0060\n4. Returns the \u0060ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder\u0060 for further configuration\n\n**Usage:**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\nvar persistence = builder.AddFilePersistence(\u0022./chat-data\u0022, \u0022json\u0022);\npersistence.AddScopedStore\u003CMyEntity\u003E(\u0022my-entities\u0022);\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n### \u0060KernelBuilderExtensions.AddIsolatedFilePersistence\u0060\nConfigures isolated file-based persistence for a kernel.\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\npublic static class KernelBuilderExtensions\n{\n    public static void AddIsolatedFilePersistence(\n        this CyrenaKernelBuilder builder, string path, Action\u003CICyrenaPersistenceBuilder\u003E configure, string extension = \u0022json\u0022);\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**What it does:**\n1. Creates \u0060FilePersistenceOptions\u0060 with the provided path and extension\n2. Creates \u0060IsolatedFilePersistenceBuilder\u0060 with its own \u0060PersistenceFS\u0060 instance\n3. Invokes the configure callback to register stores\n\n**Usage:**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\nbuilder.AddIsolatedFilePersistence(\u0022./isolated-data\u0022, persistence =\u003E\n{\n    persistence.AddScopedStore\u003CMyEntity\u003E(\u0022my-entities\u0022);\n}, \u0022json\u0022);\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n### \u0060FilePersistenceExtensions\u0060\nExtension methods on \u0060FilePersistenceOptions\u0060 for loading data from disk.\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\npublic static class FilePersistenceExtensions\n{\n    public static IEnumerable\u003CT\u003E LoadEnumerable\u003CT\u003E(this FilePersistenceOptions options, string collectionName) where T : class, IEntity;\n    public static IList\u003CT\u003E LoadList\u003CT\u003E(this FilePersistenceOptions options, string collectionName) where T : class, IEntity;\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Creates collection directory if it doesn\u0027t exist\n- Reads all \u0060*.{FileExtension}\u0060 files from the collection directory\n- Deserializes each file as JSON to type \u0060T\u0060\n- Returns empty collection if directory doesn\u0027t exist or has no files\n\n---\n\n## Usage for Extension Developers\n\nReference \u0060Cyrena.Persistence.File\u0060 to:\n1. Add file-based persistence to your application or kernel\n2. Store entities as JSON files in a directory structure\n3. Use in-memory caching with automatic disk synchronization\n\n**Example - Application-level persistence:**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\n// In Program.cs or app startup\nbuilder.UseFilePersistence(options =\u003E\n{\n    options.BaseDirectory = Path.Combine(appDataPath, \u0022CyrenaData\u0022);\n    options.FileExtension = \u0022json\u0022;\n});\n\n// Then register stores\nbuilder.AddScopedStore\u003CMyEntity\u003E(\u0022my-entities\u0022);\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**Example - Kernel-scoped persistence:**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\n// In IAssistantPlugin.LoadAsync\nvar persistence = builder.AddFilePersistence(\u0022./chat-data\u0022);\npersistence.AddScopedStore\u003CChatHistory\u003E(\u0022history\u0022);\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**Example - Isolated persistence:**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\n// In IAssistantPlugin.LoadAsync\nbuilder.AddIsolatedFilePersistence(\u0022./isolated-chat-data\u0022, persistence =\u003E\n{\n    persistence.AddScopedStore\u003CTemporaryData\u003E(\u0022temp-data\u0022);\n});\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n### Related\n- \u0060IStore\u003CT\u003E\u0060 \u2014 Generic repository contract\n- \u0060ICyrenaPersistenceBuilder\u0060 \u2014 Builder interface\n- \u0060Cyrena.Persistence.Core\u0060 \u2014 Persistence abstraction layer","Id":"cyrena-persistence-file-overview"}